SUMMARY:Panagia Fidousa (the snakes of the Virgin)\, Markopoulo
LOCATION:Markopoulo\, Kefalonia\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Between 6 and 15 August small harmless snakes with a cross-like mark appear around the church of the Dormition in Markopoulo\, above Katelios\, and are handled by the faithful during the vespers of the 14th and the liturgy of the 15th\; years when they fail to show (1940\, 1953) are remembered as bad omens. It is a pilgrimage\, not a panigiri\, and the church is tiny\, so arrive by 6pm on the 14th if you want to get inside.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kefalonia/#markopoulo-panagia-fidousa-the-snakes-of-the-virgin-markopou
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kefalonia/#markopoulo-panagia-fidousa-the-snakes-of-the-virgin-markopou
END:VEVENT
